From 223d0f111164a23e24e33428ad0ff277091736f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 14:44:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] XD Netplay v1.5.15: host-side battle timer folded into the
 format rules pin

- Word 5 of XD's Custom-1 rules record is the timer pair: s16 +0x14 minutes
  per game (the game multiplies by 60), s16 +0x16 seconds per turn; the sign
  is the switch (rules screen negates to turn OFF; enable wrappers require
  > 0); read live by the battle through the record getters. When the new
  MAIN_XD_TIMER_ENABLED is on and a rules format is picked, FormatRuleLines
  pins (game_min << 16) | turn_s instead of the stock 0xFFC4FFEC, clamped to
  the rules screen's own ranges (1..99 min, 10..99 s) so it also renders.
- Launcher (desktop and Android): a Battle timer checkbox with two number
  fields under the Format pick, default off, 60 s / 20 min; greyed for Free
  and OU, which pin no record.
- Log: 'battlestyle timer 60s/20min word=...' when live; timer= on the
  cheats line.
- XDNetplay::VERSION 1.5.15.
